      "question": "How does the Regulation define personal data?",
      "answer_type": "single_document",
      "answer_text": "For the purposes of this Regulation, 'personal data' means any information relating to an identified or identifiable natural person (\u2018data subject\u2019); an identifiable natural person is one who can be identified, directly or indirectly, in particular by reference to an identifier such as a name, an identification number, location data, an online identifier or to one or more factors specific to the physical, physiological, genetic, mental, economic, cultural or social identity of that natural person [S1][S2].",
