    {
      "question_id": "single-006",
      "question": "When are we required to carry out a data protection impact assessment?",
      "answer_type": "single_document",
      "answer_text": "A data protection impact assessment is required where a type of processing, particularly using new technologies, and taking into account the nature, scope, context, and purposes of the processing, is likely to result in a high risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons [S2]. This includes systematic and extensive evaluations of personal aspects based on automated processing, including profiling, and on which decisions are based that produce legal effects concerning the natural person or similarly significantly affect the natural person [S2]. Additionally, a data protection impact assessment is required for processing on a large scale of special categories of data or personal data relating to criminal convictions and offences [S2]. It is also required for systematic monitoring of publicly accessible areas on a large scale [S2].",
